# Odd domain in x and y with one blocking factor for all levels, which is
# allowed because the gridding region keeps the fine grids away from the
# upper x and y boundaries.  The region is aligned inward to (4,4) on level
# 0, i.e. (4:139, 4:127), and (8:279, 8:255) on level 1, and the fine
# grids are multiples of 8 there.
# Tags near the upper x boundary are outside the region and are dropped; the
# tags around x = 0.95 straddle the edge of the region.  In z the region
# spans the domain, so the partial last cell is handled as without it.
